ded, StopSign decided). The new case then performs three rounds of node1.reconnected(3)+node2.reconnected(3) with the queue drained each time, calls node2.try_become_leader() and drains again, samples all three nodes as DRIFTTRIM_BEFORE, calls node2.trim(None) inside catch_unwind and emits DRIFTTRIM_TRIM with trim_outcome (ok/err/panic), compacted_idx, accepted_idx and decided_idx of the leader, then samples all three nodes as DRIFTTRIM_AFTER.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"drift_rounds\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"REPEAT_ROUND3\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[]},{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"drift_before\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"DRIFTTRIM_BEFORE\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[]},{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"drift_trim\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"DRIFTTRIM_TRIM\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[]}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":comps,\n \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"Adds the drift-then-trim case; every previously generated case is unchanged apart from sharing one execution.\\\",\\\"No production code was modified.\\\"]}\nup={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Run the probe the trim child question asks for. The new case drifts the recorded accepted indexes with three reconnection rounds, changes the leader so that the new leader's own recorded value is inflated too, and then calls the public trim(None) on that leader with the call wrapped so a panic is reported instead of aborting the run; the samples report each node's accepted and decided index and the trim's outcome, compacted index, accepted index and decided index. The comparisons require the six-index baseline before the trim, that trim(None) reports no error for a configuration whose six indices have been decided, that the compacted index reaches six, and that the leader's decided index stays covered by its entries afterwards; if the drift reaches the trim bound the error outcome and the unchanged compacted index are the witnesses.\\\"),\n \\\"experiment\\\":exp}\njson.dump(up, open('update.json','w'), indent=1); print('written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/conse